                                "example_id": "bc73e91f-fd0c-4a09-8620-8755addb3c7d",
                                "sense_id": "70ba9a71-1a8f-305a-8da8-762689b1cb48",
                                "text": "Finally he sent the jeju (Erythrinus unitaeniatus; these fish are covered with a slippery phlegm), which pushed the man out ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be197e98-d9b8-4803-be70-3f8d5b8d5373",
                                "sense_id": "70ba9a71-1a8f-305a-8da8-762689b1cb48",
                                "text": "In the jeju, the swim bladder has a respiratory function, while in the aruana it is an hydrostatic organ. Both are physostomes, and the swim bladder is divided into 2 chambers whose walls are made up of 3 enveloping membranes or mantles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e707e866-6cc7-49d7-9ecf-10328836f6df",
                                "sense_id": "70ba9a71-1a8f-305a-8da8-762689b1cb48",
                                "text": "The jeju (Hoplerythrinus unitaeniatus) is a facultative air-breathing fish that utilizes a modified swim bladder as an ..."
